Creating an Active Directory Environment
Objective
To design and deploy a Windows Server Active Directory environment capable of managing users, security groups, permissions, policies, and client authentication in a simulated business network.

Environment
Domain Controller

DC02
Operating System: Windows Server 2025 Standard Evaluation

Client Machine: CLIENT02

Operating System: Windows 11 Pro

Domain: dericklab.local

Phase 1 - Server Deployment

Step 1
Installed Oracle VirtualBox.

Step 2
Created domain controller virtual machine: DC02

Configuration:
4 GB RAM
2 CPUs
60 GB Storage

Step 3
Installed Windows Server 2025.




Phase 2 - Active Directory

Step 4
Installed Active Directory Domain Services.
Installed supporting DNS services.

Step 5
Promoted the server to a Domain Controller.

Created domain: dericklab.local



Phase 3 - Organizational Structure

Step 6
Created Organizational Units:
Management
HR
Finance
Sales
Warehouse
IT

Step 7
Created user accounts:
mary.manager
john.hr
anna.finance
mark.sales
derick.admin

Step 8
Created security groups:
Management_Group
HR_Group
Finance_Group
Sales_Group
Warehouse_Group
IT_Admins

Step 9
Assigned users to corresponding groups.

Example:
anna.finance → Finance_Group
john.hr → HR_Group


Phase 4 - Client Deployment

Step 10
Created Windows 11 virtual machine: CLIENT02

Configuration:
Windows 11 Pro
4 GB RAM
2 CPUs
60 GB Storage
Step 11
Configured networking between CLIENT02 and DC02.

Step 12
Joined CLIENT02 to: dericklab.local

Step 13
Authenticated users through Active Directory.

Successful logins:
anna.finance
john.hr


Phase 5 - File Permissions

Step 14
Created shared folders.

Assigned permissions using security groups.

Validated access control through user accounts.

Phase 6 - Group Policy

Step 15
Created and applied Group Policy Objects.

Verified successful policy deployment to domain users.

